&lt;p&gt;Hi, we&#39;re Oscar. We&#39;re hiring a Clinical Pharmacist Supervisor - Prior Authorization to join our Pharmacy Utilization Management team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Oscar is the first health insurance company built around a full stack technology platform and a relentless focus on serving our members. We started Oscar in 2012 to create the kind of health insurance company we would want for ourselves—one that behaves like a doctor in the family.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Clinical Pharmacist Supervisor - Prior Authorization oversees a team of pharmacists performing clinical review for prior authorizations and appeals. This role will drive operational excellence, foster team development, and ensure sound, evidence-based clinical decision-making to consistently meet organizational performance objectives, regulatory standards, and quality goals.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will report into the Manager, Pharmacy Utilization Management.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work Location:&lt;/strong&gt; This position is fully remote and open to candidates residing in the U.S., &lt;strong&gt;excluding&lt;/strong&gt; Alaska; Delaware; Hawaii; Louisiana; Montana; North Dakota; Oklahoma; West Virginia; Wyoming; and U.S. Territories. Daily work is completed from your home office, with occasional travel required for team meetings and company events. #LI-Remote&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pay Transparency: &lt;/strong&gt;The base pay for this role in the states of California, Connecticut, New Jersey, New York, and Washington is: $135,792.00 - $178,227.00 per year. The base pay for this role in all other locations is: $122,212.00 - $160,404.00 per year. You are also eligible for employee benefits, participation in Oscar&#39;s unlimited vacation program, and annual performance bonuses.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage daily workflows, queue monitoring, and scheduling to ensure the pharmacist team consistently meets clinical accuracy standards and response timelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor productivity and quality metrics, providing routine 1-on-1 coaching, performance reviews, and cross-training to help team members build clinical skills, step into expanded roles, and prepare for market expansion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a clinical expert to review, troubleshoot, and resolve complex, high-priority prior authorization cases and appeals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with the Clinical Quality team on routine reviews, using audit findings to deliver constructive coaching, training, and performance support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively identify and implement process improvements, and resolve day-to-day challenges to keep the team operating efficiently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with cross-functional leadership to develop, update, and organize job aids and team training resources.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in a rotated weekend and holiday on-call schedule to monitor queues and offer team support when needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Compliance with all applicable laws and regulations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Other duties as assigned&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Doctor of Pharmacy Degree.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Active, unrestricted pharmacist license.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of experience in managed care performing clinical review/utilization management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1+ year(s) of people or project management experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus points:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing a team of clinical pharmacists performing clinical review/utilization management operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing and managing key performance indicators/metrics for an operational team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong clinical skills and experience applying clinical criteria in a clinical review setting.&lt;/li&gt;
