&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Accreditation Implementation:&lt;/strong&gt; Direct the full end-to-end execution of updated accreditation standards affecting Utilization Management (UM) policies. Partner closely with the Quality team and key organizational stakeholders to ensure seamless alignment and robust compliance with NCQA standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;NCQA Survey Readiness &amp;amp; Response: &lt;/strong&gt;Organize and maintain readiness documentation and evidence of compliance. Direct audit and survey preparation for NCQA state and triennial surveys.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Accreditation Compliance Oversight:&lt;/strong&gt; Act as the primary business partner and lead coordinator for NCQA UM Subcommittee initiatives. Collaborate seamlessly with the Quality team and Operations to deliver quarterly UM performance reporting that upholds Accreditation compliance, providing strategic transparency to enhance program adherence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Subcommittee Collaboration:&lt;/strong&gt; Lead engagement with Operations leadership to pinpoint critical performance metrics, emerging trends, key risks, and accomplishments for quarterly Subcommittee reporting; partner closely with Quality to refine and finalize review materials.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Programmatic Governance:&lt;/strong&gt; Track policy changes, approvals, and outstanding actions to support accreditation readiness and documentation integrity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stakeholder Alignment: &lt;/strong&gt;Lead the end-to-end management of cross-functional implementations/projects, including project plan creation, stakeholder engagement, managing cross-functional relationships to drive collaboration, edge case mitigation, and on-time completion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaboration: &lt;/strong&gt;Partners across internal and external stakeholder teams to design and execute proactive program, communication, and implementation strategies, driving effective change management and risk mitigation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Management:&lt;/strong&gt; May oversee team members directly as well as mentors team members and promotes colleagues&#39; growth and professional development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of experience in health plan operations, utilization management, quality, compliance, accreditation, regulatory affairs, or a related function.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of direct experience supporting NCQA accreditation, including standards interpretation, implementation, survey readiness, audit response, or ongoing compliance monitoring.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of experience with end to end project management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of experience in regulatory implementation, audits, and compliance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of experience in designing and improving workflows as well as standing up accompanying operating and technical procedure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to present findings, risks, and recommendations to stakeholders and leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to build collaborative relationships across operations, compliance, regulatory, quality, data, and technical teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly organized, detail-oriented, and able to manage multiple priorities and deadlines independently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with Microsoft Excel, PowerPoint, Google Docs, Google Sheets, and project-management or documentation tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus points:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in healthcare administration, public health, nursing, business, or a related field; equivalent combination of education and relevant experience may be considered.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience / background in a fast-paced operations environment&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;PMP Certifications or Program Management Certifications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lean/Six Sigma Certifications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Healthcare experience (Health Insurance, Health Systems, or Healthcare Consulting)&lt;/li&gt;
