&lt;p&gt;Hi, we&#39;re Oscar. We&#39;re hiring a Manager, Program Implementation Oversight and Monitoring to join our team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Oscar is the first health insurance company built around a full stack technology platform and a relentless focus on serving our members. We started Oscar in 2012 to create the kind of health insurance company we would want for ourselves—one that behaves like a doctor in the family.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Manager, Program Implementation Oversight &amp;amp; Monitoring leads the post-implementation oversight, compliance monitoring, risk assessment, and remediation activities for Utilization Management. This role is responsible for ensuring regulatory and operational changes function as intended after launch, identifying emerging compliance risks, driving root cause analysis and corrective actions, and maintaining clear documentation for leadership, regulatory, and audit needs.This individual translates regulatory requirements into sustainable monitoring processes and drives accountability for timely issue resolution.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will report into the Senior Manager, UM Regulatory Operations&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work Location: &lt;/strong&gt;This position is based in our New York City, NY office, requiring a hybrid work schedule with 3 days of in-office work per week. Thursdays are a required in-office day for team meetings and events, while your other two office days are flexible to suit your schedule. #LI-Hybrid&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pay Transparency: &lt;/strong&gt;The base pay for this role is: $111,780 - $146,711 per year. You are also eligible for employee benefits and participation in Oscar&#39;s unlimited vacation program.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Regulatory Data Metrics Management: &lt;/strong&gt;Manage the complete lifecycle of regulatory compliance, reporting, and public disclosures on an annual and ad-hoc basis. Partner with cross-functional teams to capture regulatory specifications and assess their downstream operational, data, and public posting implications. Create precise data requests for key partners, rigorously validate incoming datasets, populate sanctioned reporting templates, and seamlessly execute annual publications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Post-Launch Audit and Implementation Oversight:&lt;/strong&gt; Establish and manage post-launch audit processes for regulatory and operational implementations, tracking completed changes to validate that processes, systems, communications, and workflows function as designed while identifying defects, compliance gaps, or unintended operational impacts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Central Escalation &amp;amp; Incident Tracking: &lt;/strong&gt;Coordinate remediation plans with accountable stakeholders, monitor progress through resolution, and document validation activities, findings, corrective actions, and final outcomes to support ongoing regulatory readiness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead Regulatory Compliance Initiatives: &lt;/strong&gt;Conduct root cause analyses to identify contributing factors, systemic drivers, and compliance-improvement opportunities; partner with stakeholder teams to develop actionable corrective actions; consolidate findings, ownership, actions, and outcomes for leadership and governance reporting; and identify recurring themes to recommend targeted process, policy, workflow, or training improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Real-Time Compliance Monitoring and Risk Management:&lt;/strong&gt; Design, implement, and maintain a compliance-monitoring framework for key utilization management and insurance operations processes, including mechanisms to identify emerging issues, control failures, and compliance risks; define key risk and performance indicators for oversight and escalation; and track recurring risks and pain points to inform strategic action and leadership reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stakeholder Alignment: &lt;/strong&gt;Lead the end-to-end management of cross-functional implementations/projects, including project plan creation, stakeholder engagement, managing cross-functional relationships to drive collaboration, edge case mitigation, and on-time completion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaboration: &lt;/strong&gt;Collaboratively works with all relevant internal and external stakeholder groups to formulate proactive implementation, communications, and program strategies for successful change management and risk mitigation initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Management:&lt;/strong&gt; May oversee team members directly as well as mentors team members and promotes colleagues&#39; growth and professional development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Other:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;em&gt; Other duties as assigned&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A bachelor&#39;s degree or 4+ years commensurate experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of work experience in Utilization Management operations, health insurance, and/or consulting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of experience with end to end project management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of experience in regulatory implementation, audits, and compliance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of experience in designing and improving workflows as well as standing up accompanying operating and technical procedure&lt;/li&gt;
