&lt;p&gt;Hi, we&#39;re Oscar. We&#39;re hiring a Operations Analyst, Plan Loading to join our Claims and Benefits Configuration Team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Oscar is the first health insurance company built around a full stack technology platform and a relentless focus on serving our members. We started Oscar in 2012 to create the kind of health insurance company we would want for ourselves—one that behaves like a doctor in the family.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Analyst, Configuration supports incoming projects and work designed to improve the consistency, accuracy, and efficiency of Oscar processes through system configuration. Through collaboration with stakeholders in the organization and gaining an understanding of Oscar&#39;s platform capabilities, this role ensures information is loaded accurately and efficiently.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will report into the Senior Operations Manager, Benefit Coinfiguration.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work Location: &lt;/strong&gt;This position is fully remote and open to candidates residing in the U.S., excluding Alaska; Delaware; Hawaii; Louisiana; Montana; North Dakota; Oklahoma; West Virginia; Wyoming; and U.S. Territories. Daily work is completed from your home office, with occasional travel required for team meetings and company events. #LI-Remote&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pay Transparency: &lt;/strong&gt;The base pay for this role in the states of California, Connecticut, New Jersey, New York, and Washington is: $62,100 - $81,506.25 per year. The base pay for this role in all other locations is: $55,890 - $73,335.63 per year. You are also eligible for employee benefits, participation in Oscar&#39;s unlimited vacation program and annual performance bonuses.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform detailed oriented work with a high level of accuracy and adherence to all QA/QC protocols&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of designs, builds, and configuration workflows and utilize this knowledge to develop insights into opportunities for workflow improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
