&lt;p&gt;Hi, we&#39;re Oscar. We&#39;re hiring a Product Designer to join our Product Design team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Oscar is the first health insurance company built around a full stack technology platform and a relentless focus on serving our members. We started Oscar in 2012 to create the kind of health insurance company we would want for ourselves - one that behaves like a doctor in the family.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll design the tools that help Oscar build and manage provider networks so members can find the care they need. You’ll work with the teams that recruit and contract with providers, check their credentials, and keep their records accurate. You’ll also help improve how providers join Oscar’s network, complete routine tasks, and get support.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hands-on Product Designer role on Oscar’s Internal Tools team. You’ll work with Product, Engineering, Research, Data, and Network Operations to understand how people work across tools, then design, test, and ship improvements. Work could include helping teams see where their network needs more providers, track contracts through each step, or find and correct errors in provider records before they affect other work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role reports to a Product Design Director.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work Location:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This position is based in our Marina Del Rey office, requiring a hybrid work schedule with 3 days of in-office work per week. Thursdays are a required in-office day for team meetings and events, while your other two office days are flexible to suit your schedule. #LI-Hybrid&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pay Transparency:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The base pay for this role is: $123,372.00 - $161,925.75 per year. You are also eligible for employee benefits, participation in Oscar&#39;s unlimited vacation program, company equity grants, and annual performance bonuses.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Observe and interview Network staff and providers. Map tasks and handoffs across tools to find where people lose time, repeat work, or lack the information they need to act.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own design for defined features and workflows from discovery through delivery. Work with Product, Engineering, and other designers to define the problem, choose what to test, and agree on how to measure success.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make complex information easier to act on. Design clear ways to compare provider performance, costs, or contract terms and see what needs attention next.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve the steps providers take to join the network and get support. Use research to identify where clearer information or self-service can help.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Explore options in existing tools before proposing something new. Build and test working prototypes, using approved AI tools where they help you learn faster.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design accessible web interfaces with clear states, errors, and recovery steps. Use Oscar’s design system and work with engineers to check the details in the shipped experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review feedback and product data after launch to see whether the work made tasks easier and where to improve next.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comply with all applicable laws and regulations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform other duties as assigned.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of experience in product or UX design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Two or more examples of designing and shipping complex software. Show how research, prototypes, and visual and interaction design informed the work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years working directly with partners across functions to make design decisions and deliver work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus points:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing internal tools, enterprise software, or other products that help people work with complex data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in healthcare, insurance, provider operations, or another regulated industry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience observing users at work and testing prototypes with them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working within an established platform or design system and improving workflows that span tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using AI-assisted tools to explore ideas or build and test prototypes.&lt;/li&gt;
