&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with SIU and Medical Economics to understand business needs, translate them into data science solutions, and independently manage stakeholder relationships for your projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own projects end-to-end, including problem definition, technical design, implementation, validation, and ongoing evaluation and improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interact and collaborate closely with data and business counterparts across functional areas&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with your team and manager to identify opportunities and contribute to the fraud data science roadmap and longer-term technical direction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide mentorship and technical guidance to junior data scientists.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Compliance with all applicable laws and regulations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Other duties as assigned.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of experience in data science or another quantitative technical field, which may include academia.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience using SQL and Python to query, manipulate, and analyze data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years experience building data models, using more advanced analytics methods, statistical modeling, and/or data processing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience applying supervised or unsupervised machine learning techniques, such as predictive modeling, anomaly detection, clustering, or graph/network analysis, to identify potential fraud in healthcare, insurance, financial services, or other industries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
