&lt;li&gt;Set and lead the strategic vision, roadmap, governance, and ongoing administration for Oscar’s intranet, ensuring it advances company strategy, reinforces culture, and serves as a trusted, intuitive destination for employee information and communications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain intranet content standards, editorial processes, information architecture, publishing workflows, ownership models, and governance practices that improve content quality, consistency, findability, and alignment to company priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create, edit, and manage strategic intranet content—including company updates, evergreen resources, leader communications, FAQs, change-management materials, employee tools, and culture content—that helps employees understand, connect to, and act on Oscar’s priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with cross-functional stakeholders and senior leaders to assess strategic objectives, employee impact, audience needs, timing, sensitivity, and channel requirements; provide recommendations on messaging, format, placement, sequencing, and ongoing content maintenance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use intranet and channel analytics, employee feedback, search behavior, and content performance data to identify opportunities to improve employee understanding, engagement, usability, content relevance, and the overall employee experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Draft, edit, and provide strategic writing support for internal communications that advance company strategy and culture, including executive and leader communications, companywide announcements, newsletters, talking points, presentations, manager toolkits, and other employee-facing materials.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Compliance with all applicable laws and regulations&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Other duties as assigned&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Communications, English, Journalism, Public Relations, Marketing, Business, or a related discipline; equivalent practical experience may be considered.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of experience in internal communications, employee communications, corporate communications, content strategy, editorial, digital communications, intranet management, or a related discipline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience managing or substantially contributing to an employee intranet, knowledge base, digital content platform, or comparable channel.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience writing and editing clear, audience-appropriate content for varied employee audiences and business needs.&lt;/li&gt;
