&lt;p&gt;In close partnership with Network Strategy &amp;amp; Performance, Regional Actuarial, Medical Economics, and Data teams, the Senior Manager evaluates new network strategies, identifies financial risks and opportunities, and strengthens analytical methods and tools. You will translate complex analyses into clear recommendations and reporting, helping business and operational leaders make informed decisions about provider reimbursement and network initiatives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will report into the Director, Actuarial.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work Location:&lt;/strong&gt; This position is fully remote and open to candidates residing in the U.S., &lt;strong&gt;excluding&lt;/strong&gt; Alaska; Delaware; Hawaii; Louisiana; Montana; North Dakota; Oklahoma; West Virginia; Wyoming; and U.S. Territories. Daily work is completed from your home office, with occasional travel required for team meetings and company events. #LI-Remote&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pay Transparency: &lt;/strong&gt;The base pay for this role in the states of California, Connecticut, New Jersey, New York, and Washington is: $163,944 - $215,176 per year. The base pay for this role in all other locations is: $147,549 - $193,658 per year. You are also eligible for employee benefits, participation in Oscar&#39;s unlimited vacation program and annual performance bonuses.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own end-to-end financial analysis for complex, high-impact provider negotiations, evaluating proposed reimbursement rates, contract terms, and alternative structures to inform negotiation strategy and decision-making.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In collaboration with Network Strategy &amp;amp; Performance, provide recommendations and thought partnership based on financial analysis and actuarial principles related to new network strategies and initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain contracting guardrails, unit cost targets, and financial benchmarks aligned with business objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strengthen analytical methods and processes for evaluating provider contracts, establishing consistent modeling standards and partnering with Regional Actuarial, Medical Economics, and Data teams to improve tools, reporting, and analytical efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and quantify financial risks and affordability opportunities through analysis of provider reimbursement, utilization, medical cost trends, and competitive benchmarks; recommend actions to improve network financial performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and deliver detailed reports, presentations, and dashboards that distill complex network medical economics insights for internal stakeholders, project teams, and business unit leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain strong working relationships with key business and operational leaders (e.g., Network, Market P&amp;amp;L, Payment Integrity, Claim Operations) to ensure analytic solutions meet their needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Other duties as assigned.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in a STEM field, or 4 years commensurate experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of quantitative analysis in the healthcare industry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience in health insurance / payer analytics, with an understanding of medical claims data (e.g., CPT/HCPCS, ICD-10, DRGs) and standard healthcare industry data sources.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus points:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication, collaboration, and relationship-building skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong process management skills, with experience streamlining workflows and driving operational efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience translating between clinical, business, and analytic vocabularies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with ACA-specific healthcare laws, regulations, and compliance requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Associate or Fellow of the Society of Actuaries (SOA), or on the track to become one.&lt;/li&gt;
