&lt;p&gt;Hi, we&#39;re Oscar. We&#39;re hiring a Senior User Experience Researcher to join our Insights &amp;amp; Analytics team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Oscar is the first health insurance company built around a full stack technology platform and a relentless focus on serving our members. We started Oscar in 2012 to create the kind of health insurance company we would want for ourselves - one that behaves like a doctor in the family.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Oscar is building a centralized Insights and Analytics function within Technology, bringing together User Experience Research, Data Science, Analytics, and Market Research to inform how we learn, decide, and build. Our UX Researchers ground product, service, and business decisions in the experiences, behaviors, and needs of consumers, members, brokers, providers, and internal users across Oscar’s Tech Pillars and family of companies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will independently lead qualitative, quantitative, and mixed-methods research to clarify complex problems, reduce risk, and shape strategy. You will partner across disciplines to translate insights into clear priorities, better workflows, and confident decisions. Success requires comfort with ambiguity, a clear research point of view, and the ability to connect human insights to business needs. You will also strengthen how Oscar plans, conducts, shares, and reuses research, including thoughtful use of AI-enabled tools.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will report into the Associate Director, User Experience Research.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work Location: &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a remote position, open to candidates who reside in: San Francisco, CA. You will be fully remote; however, our approach to work may adapt over time. Future models could potentially involve a hybrid presence at the hub office associated with your metro area. #LI-Remote&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pay Transparency: &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The base pay for this role is: $163,944.00 - $215,176.50 per year. You are also eligible for employee benefits, participation in Oscar&#39;s unlimited vacation program, company equity grants, and annual performance bonuses.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead end-to-end research studies, including scoping, study design, recruiting strategy, moderation, analysis, synthesis, and shareout.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate ambiguous questions into research plans that clarify methods, audiences, risks, and decision points.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct research across Oscar’s multi-sided healthcare ecosystem, including consumers, members, brokers, providers, and internal users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply qualitative, quantitative, and mixed methods to generate evidence that is rigorous, actionable, and fit for the decision at hand.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product, Design, Engineering, Data, Operations, Clinical, Strategy, and Insurance Product teams to shape problem definition, roadmap planning, prioritization, product strategy, and launch readiness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Distill research into strategic recommendations that help teams decide what to build, improve, prioritize, or stop doing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strengthen Oscar’s research operations, including intake, planning, recruiting, consent, compliance, repositories, templates, and vendor workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use AI-enabled tools thoughtfully to accelerate research planning, analysis, synthesis, and knowledge reuse while upholding rigor, privacy, compliance, and human judgment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advance ethical and inclusive research practices in a regulated healthcare environment, including privacy, security, accessibility, language, incentives, and hard-to-reach population considerations as we comply with all applicable laws and regulations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help mature Oscar’s research practice by introducing useful methods, tools, documentation patterns, and industry learnings, including mentoring junior researchers and research-adjacent partners where appropriate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Compliance with all applicable laws and regulations.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Other duties as assigned.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of hands-on user research, product research, design research, or applied research.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience independently leading research studies with moderate to high complexity and cross-functional stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated skill collecting, analyzing, and synthesizing human behavioral data to inform product, service, or business decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using qualitative and quantitative methods, with strong judgment about which method fits the decision at hand.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience turning ambiguous questions into clear research plans, actionable insights, and strategic recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience communicating research findings through compelling artifacts, frameworks, presentations, or workshops.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with Product, Design, Engineering, Data, Operations, Strategy, or other cross-functional partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort working within ethical, privacy, compliance, or operational constraints.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus points:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience conducting research in healthcare, health insurance, benefits, financial services, or another regulated industry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience researching multi-sided ecosystems, such as members/consumers, brokers, providers, internal operators, or B2B2C products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Masters or Ph.D. in Human-Computer Interaction, Cognitive Psychology, Information Science, Anthropology, Sociology, STS, or related technical field, or 2+ years of equivalent work experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Spanish language proficiency. Experience conducting discovery research and testing features with English and Spanish speaking participants, as well as analyzing consumer insights from diverse linguistic backgrounds.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Travel Required:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Up to 5%&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;This is an authentic Oscar Health job opportunity.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
