&lt;p&gt;Hi, we&#39;re Oscar. We&#39;re hiring a Senior User Experience Researcher to join our Insights &amp;amp; Analytics team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Oscar is the first health insurance company built around a full stack technology platform and a relentless focus on serving our members. We started Oscar in 2012 to create the kind of health insurance company we would want for ourselves - one that behaves like a doctor in the family.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Oscar is building a centralized Insights and Analytics function within Technology, bringing together User Experience Research, Data Science, Analytics, and Market Research to inform how we learn, decide, and build. Our UX Researchers ground product, service, and business decisions in the experiences, behaviors, and needs of consumers, members, brokers, providers, and internal users across Oscar’s Tech Pillars and family of companies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will independently lead qualitative, quantitative, and mixed-methods research to clarify complex problems, reduce risk, and shape strategy. You will partner across disciplines to translate insights into clear priorities, better workflows, and confident decisions. Success requires comfort with ambiguity, a clear research point of view, and the ability to connect human insights to business needs. You will also strengthen how Oscar plans, conducts, shares, and reuses research, including thoughtful use of AI-enabled tools.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will report into the Associate Director, User Experience Research.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work Location:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This position is based in our Los Angeles (Marina del Rey) office, requiring a hybrid work schedule with 3 days of in-office work per week. Thursdays are a required in-office day for team meetings and events, while your other two office days are flexible to suit your schedule. #LI-Hybrid&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pay Transparency:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The base pay for this role is: $163,944.00 - $215,176.50 per year. You are also eligible for employee benefits, participation in Oscar&#39;s unlimited vacation program, company equity grants, and annual performance bonuses.&lt;/p&gt;
