&lt;p&gt;Hi, we&#39;re Oscar. We&#39;re hiring a Staff Product Manager, Personalization to join our Clinical Product team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Oscar is the first health insurance company built around a full stack technology platform and a relentless focus on serving our members. We started Oscar in 2012 to create the kind of health insurance company we would want for ourselves—one that behaves like a doctor in the family.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Oscar is hiring a Staff Product Manager to join our Clinical Product team and build the shared platform behind personalized care guidance and navigation. Come help members make informed decisions about their health and follow through on the care they need.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Staff Product Manager, Personalization, you will help build Oscar Health’s personalization platform, using longitudinal member context, real-time behavioral signals, predictive models, and LLMs to forecast what is likely to happen for each member and identify the most useful next action. We combine longitudinal member context with real-time behavioral signals to forecast what is likely to happen for a member and determine the most useful next action for the member to engage across web and app, our member facing health AI agent (Oscar), tools used by Oscar teammates during member conversations, and intentional outbound engagement. The work includes predictive modeling; creating a catalogue of action and journey options to engage members with; recommendation and ranking systems; experimentation and measurement; and practical use of AI and LLMs to interpret context, support recommendations, and generate tailored experiences. We are looking for people who have built and operated personalization, recommender, ranking, predictive-modeling, search, decisioning, or applied-AI systems at meaningful scale. This is a unique opportunity to build an advanced platform leveraging the latest capabilities at an AI-forward company that owns its technology stack, with tangible benefits for members’ health and lives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will report into a Director of Product.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work Location: &lt;/strong&gt;This is a remote position, open to candidates who reside in: San Francisco, CA. You will be fully remote; however, our approach to work may adapt over time. Future models could potentially involve a hybrid presence at the hub office associated with your metro area. #LI-Remote&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pay Transparency: &lt;/strong&gt;The base pay for this role is: $180,504.00 - $236,911.50 per year. You are also eligible for employee benefits, participation in Oscar&#39;s unlimited vacation program, company equity grants, and annual performance bonuses.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the catalog of care options that powers personalized recommendations for members. Drive adoption across Oscar teams and measure the impact on member outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define, prioritize, and execute on the most impactful problems to solve for a portfolio of product investments, informed by member research and analysis of care journeys, ensuring alignment with Oscar’s overall business goals, market demands, and competitive landscape.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct thorough and continuous market and competitive analysis to identify new opportunities, anticipate industry trends, and translate these insights into actionable outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee the entire product lifecycle for multiple product lines, including the personalization platform and its first clinical journeys, from ideation and conception through development, launch, and post-launch optimization, ensuring impact is delivered on multiple cross-company business objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the primary communication link and strategic partner between product teams and business leadership, ensuring clear, consistent updates, strategic alignment, and effective two-way communication regarding product plans, progress, and strategic direction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define, track, and report on Key Performance Indicators (KPIs) for the entire product portfolio, including affordability, care completion and member experience, analyzing performance data and customer feedback to drive continuous improvement and data-driven decision-making.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Independently identify, diagnose, and resolve complex strategic or executional challenges across teams and domains, demonstrating exceptional problem-solving, negotiation, and influencing skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Compliance with all applicable laws and regulations.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Other duties as assigned.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of experience collaborating cross-functionally among engineers, designers, operations experts, and others in a Product Management or Product Management-adjacent role,&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus points:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with healthcare claims, clinical workflows, care navigation, or health insurance economics, including how coverage, cost and access barriers affect members’ ability to get appropriate care and follow through on treatment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience owning recommender, search, ads, ML-platform, or applied-AI product capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort in working in highly collaborative environments while ensuring the team is always driving towards a decision.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent analytical and quantitative skills; proven experience using data to identify opportunities, test hypotheses and evaluate success, including investigating individual member experiences and broader population patterns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience as an end-to-end thinker; the ability to look at a problem and create a solution all the way from top-level goals to smaller details.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to influence and manage stakeholders at all levels and experience working across all levels of leadership using strong communication and structured thinking.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Travel Required&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Up to 5%&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;This is an authentic Oscar Health job opportunity.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
